{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory was strong in psychiatric risk management, medication non-coercion, low-stimulation family coaching, escalation to 120/110 when the patient began pushing/running, and eventual hospital handoff. However, the authored somatic responsibility-chain item on sinus arrhythmia/tachycardia red-flag stratification was never completed in any patient-visible plan despite the doctor making testing/ECG information actionable in workspace queries. That is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain omission, which caps the grade at 2 even though several high-order communication and real-world execution points were completed.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00567",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave executable post-handoff steps for contact information, going home, and next-day nurse/doctor follow-up.",
        "quote": "今晚你回家睡，手机开着"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00581",
        "explanation": "The caregiver confirmed obtaining the ward contact card and understanding that the ward would handle observation and medication.",
        "quote": "拿到一张联系卡/小纸条了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The psychiatric handoff and next-day family actions were traceable and executable, but the episode remained questionable because the cardiac/somatic red-flag thread was not explicitly closed and the final caregiver question did not receive a further doctor response.",
